# Pipeline router

When the user’s message matches a **pipeline trigger**, run the linked **playbook** end-to-end for **one** scoped unit (e.g. one Jira Epic key). Do not improvise a different procedure—follow the playbook file.

**Benchmark mode (optional tokens, all epic pipelines below):** When **both** **`benchmark_suite=<suite_id>`** and **`benchmark_attempt=<n>`** appear on the **same line** as the trigger, durable + temp paths resolve to the **shadow tree** under `.cursor/benchmark/runs/<suite_id>/attempt-<nn>/shadow/<KEY>/` (**`{EpicDir}`** per [docs/benchmark-contract.md](../../docs/benchmark-contract.md)) — **never** write QA artifacts under `epics/<KEY>/` for that run. When either token is omitted, default is **production**: `epics/<KEY>/`.

## Trigger → pipeline

- **`EPIC-PREP:`** + Epic key (e.g. `EPIC-PREP: CRT-1234`; optional `repo=` for Bitbucket prep search — Cloud `workspace/slug`, internal Stash `PROJECT_KEY/repo_slug` e.g. `BRO/xt`; optional **`focus=`**; optional **`benchmark_suite=`** + **`benchmark_attempt=`** for shadow tree) → pipeline id `epic-prep` → playbook [`.cursor/pipelines/epic-prep.md`](../pipelines/epic-prep.md). **Schema v4** `obligations_proposed[]` via per-requirement subprocesses; **`epic_prep_verify.py`** before finalize; **no** CRTQA / downstream artefacts as input; delete `{EpicDir}temp/` when done.
- **`COVERAGE:`** + Epic key (e.g. `COVERAGE: CRT-593`; optional `repo=` for Bitbucket — overrides epic-ref / project default; same token shapes as EPIC-PREP; optional `focus=...` free-text verification focus; optional **`benchmark_suite=`** + **`benchmark_attempt=`**) → pipeline id `coverage` → playbook [`.cursor/pipelines/coverage.md`](../pipelines/coverage.md). Requires **`-ref.json` v4** with obligations; **schema v2** `obligations_coverage`; section subprocesses + **`coverage_verify.py`**; delete `{EpicDir}temp/` when done.
- **`ANALYSE:`** + Epic key (e.g. `ANALYSE: CRT-642`; optional **`known_issues=yes`** default off; optional **`include_closed=yes`** with known_issues; optional **`resolve=no`** audit-only; optional **`benchmark_suite=`** + **`benchmark_attempt=`**) → pipeline id `analysis` → playbook [`.cursor/pipelines/analysis.md`](../pipelines/analysis.md). **Requires** `-coverage.json`; **schema v2** gaps + `exploration_suppressed[]`; **`analysis_verify.py`** before emit; Known issue **`>`** mutation only when **`known_issues=yes`**; delete `{EpicDir}temp/` when done.
- **`TEST-DISCOVER:`** + Epic key (e.g. `TEST-DISCOVER: CRT-639`; optional **`benchmark_suite=`** + **`benchmark_attempt=`**; optional **`crtqa_index=yes`**; optional **`proceed`** after Phase **0** hard stop; optional **`skip_cold_gate=yes`**; optional **`dxtrade5_creds=`** / **`webbroker_creds=`** — **secrets MUST NOT** enter durable JSON; **`fe_exploration_waived=yes`** only after Phase **0b** FE stop + operator ack; **no** `adaptive_creds=` — Adaptive uses CTQA shared principal when ref marks affected) → pipeline id `test-discover` → playbook [`.cursor/pipelines/test-discover.md`](../pipelines/test-discover.md). **Phase 0:** machine gates + **0b/0c** FE credential + post-login Chrome smoke ([`docs/fe-ui-probe-contract.json`](../../docs/fe-ui-probe-contract.json)); **`fe_credentials.supplied` ≠ authenticated**. **Recommended operator prep:** **`/crtqa-console start`** then **`/crtqa-env`**. **Hard stop:** no **`-discover.json`** until **`proceed`** or waiver. Step **E:** fixture probes capped by **`fe_ui_sessions`** (no **`probe_executed`** on FE kinds when **`shell_only`**/waived); Adaptive Chrome when **`client_shell_impact.adaptive`** affected. Steps **0**→**G**, **`discover_verify.py`**; delete `{EpicDir}temp/` when done.
- **`TEST-PRECON:`** + Epic key (e.g. `TEST-PRECON: CRT-639`; optional **`benchmark_suite=`** + **`benchmark_attempt=`**; optional **`proceed`** / **`skip_cold_gate=yes`**; optional **`dxtrade5_creds=`** / **`webbroker_creds=`** — not in durable JSON; **`fe_exploration_waived=yes`** after **0b** ack) → pipeline id `test-precon` → playbook [`.cursor/pipelines/test-precon.md`](../pipelines/test-precon.md). **v4 depth:** [`docs/exploration-depth-ladder.json`](../../docs/exploration-depth-ladder.json) — **0c** = smoke; **Phase 4R/4D/4C** = **`precon_drill`** (replay discover + navigated views); **`precon_verify.py --discover`** (max **3** cluster loops). Schema v4 **`-precon.json`** + **`-precon.md`**; delete `{EpicDir}temp/` when done.
- **`TEST-PREP:`** + Epic key (e.g. `TEST-PREP: CRT-639`; optional **`draft_profile=teaching`** default **`crtqa_outline`**; optional **`shape_ref=benchmark`** **only with both** **`benchmark_suite=`** + **`benchmark_attempt=`**; optional **`draft_split=per_check|per_bundle`**; optional **`map_only=yes`**; optional **`discover_override=yes`**; optional benchmark / FE cred tokens / waiver / **`proceed`** / **`skip_cold_gate=yes`**) → pipeline id `test-prep` → playbook [`.cursor/pipelines/test-prep.md`](../pipelines/test-prep.md). Greenfield; **8a** → **0c smoke** → **8a½ plan + case_outline** → **8a¾** → **8b** (per bundle or per check) → **8c merge** → emit. Verifier: **`plan` / `explore` / `draft` / `merge` / `tests`**. **`-tests.json`** schema v4; delete `{EpicDir}temp/` when done.
- **`CLOSE:`** + Epic key (e.g. `CLOSE: CRT-639`; optional **`heal=no`** default heal on; optional **`benchmark_suite=`** + **`benchmark_attempt=`**) → pipeline id `close` → playbook [`.cursor/pipelines/close.md`](../pipelines/close.md). **Documentation-only** integrity ladder (L0–L4) after **TEST-PREP**; requires `{EpicDir}<KEY>-ref.json`, `-coverage.json`, `-discover.json`, `-precon.json`, `-tests.json`; **no** MCP/creds; **one subprocess per bundle per level**; finalize whitelist corrections; regenerate four root `.md`; **archive always** to `{EpicDir}context/` (including `-close.json`); delete `{EpicDir}temp/` when done.
- **`PUBLIC-SCRUB:`** (optional `version=X.Y.Z`; optional `source=develop` default or `source=main`) → pipeline id `public-scrub` → playbook [`.cursor/pipelines/public-scrub.md`](../pipelines/public-scrub.md). Sanitizes the tree for public export on branch **`release` only**; merges `origin/develop` or `origin/main` into `release`, tiers A–D, `.agents/` layer, semver manifest, V1/V2 verification; **never** commit scrub results on `main` or `develop`. Ephemeral: `automation/temp/public-scrub/` then delete before commit.
- **`SYNC:`** (optional `scope=full` default, or `scope=pipelines` / `scope=prompts` / `scope=templates` / `scope=tools` / `scope=mcp`) → pipeline id `sync` → playbook [`.cursor/pipelines/sync.md`](../pipelines/sync.md). Reconciles router, harness-map, AGENTS, README, root **HOW-TO.md**, qa-artifacts, prompts, templates, automation tools, MCP doc parity (**postgres-ctqa** snippet in **`automation/tools/tunnel/README.md`**), rules inventory per [harness-maintenance.mdc](harness-maintenance.mdc); **only** on **`develop`** or **`main`** — **not** on **`release`**. Ephemeral: `automation/temp/sync/` then delete before finishing.

## Hard rules

1. **One epic key** (or one primary scope) per pipeline run unless the user explicitly widens scope.
2. **No secrets** in repo files (passwords, session cookies, tokens)—see [harness-maintenance.mdc](harness-maintenance.mdc) and Atlassian rules.
3. **Temp folder**: for `epic-prep`, `coverage`, `analysis`, `test-discover`, `test-precon`, `test-prep`, and `close`, use only **`{EpicDir}temp/`** (`epics/<KEY>/temp/` in production, or shadow-tree `.../shadow/<KEY>/temp/` when `benchmark_suite=` + `benchmark_attempt=` are set — [docs/benchmark-contract.md](../../docs/benchmark-contract.md)). **Before finishing** (success or abort after temp was created), **delete** `temp/` entirely. Pre-**CLOSE** durable artifacts live at `{EpicDir}` root; post-**CLOSE** JSON under `{EpicDir}context/` with four human `.md` at root (see [`.cursor/pipelines/close.md`](../pipelines/close.md)). Durable JSON must not reference paths under `temp/`. For **`public-scrub`** and **`sync`**, scratch only under **`automation/temp/public-scrub/`** and **`automation/temp/sync/`** respectively; delete those folders before the run is complete.
4. **Downstream trust**: later pipelines should treat **`synthesis`** and **`traversal.xt_refs`** as provisional until steps 3.4 / 3.6 in the playbook have run; **`requirements[]`** entries are tool-backed when `snippet_text` / `page_id` are filled from Yogi/MCP, not invented. **`implementation.hits`** on the epic ref are tool-backed when populated from Bitbucket MCP in EPIC-PREP step **5b**; COVERAGE renumbers/dedupes them in phase **7**.
5. **`PUBLIC-SCRUB:`** — **only** branch **`release`** may receive scrub edits and commits. **One** completed run = **one** `release` commit (plus optional tag). Do not scrub or commit scrub output on **`main`** or **`develop`**.
6. **`SYNC:`** — run harness reconciliation on **`develop`** or **`main`** only. Do not use **`SYNC:`** on **`release`** (use **`PUBLIC-SCRUB:`** there).

T1 context: [docs/harness-map.json](docs/harness-map.json) `match_any_package` ids — `product_fork_platform`, `corner_qa_process`, `corner_platform_map`, `crtqa_env` (`/crtqa-env`), `jq_json`, `deliverable_shape`, `figma_design`, `yogi_requirement`, `epic_ref` (`EPIC-PREP`), `coverage_pipeline` (`COVERAGE`), `analysis_pipeline` (`ANALYSE`), `test_discover_pipeline` (`TEST-DISCOVER`), `test_precon_pipeline` (`TEST-PRECON`), `test_prep_pipeline` (`TEST-PREP`), `close_pipeline` (`CLOSE`), `public_scrub_pipeline` (`PUBLIC-SCRUB`), `sync_pipeline` (`SYNC`).
